.\" Manual page for sentinel-dns.
.TH SENTINEL-DNS 1 "2026" "sentinel-dns 0.2.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
sentinel-dns \- passive DNS exfiltration and DGA detection at the resolver
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B sentinel-dns
.B analyze
.I file.pcap ...
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B sentinel-dns
.B watch
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B sentinel-dns
.B selftest
.br
.B sentinel-dns
.B config
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B sentinel-dns
reads pcap data \(em an offline capture or a live
.BR tcpdump (1)
pipe \(em extracts DNS questions, and scores each client's behavior inside
rolling time windows. Alerts are one JSON object per line on stdout. A
single unusual domain is never enough: an alert requires a window score at
or above
.I score_threshold
for
.I windows_before_alert
consecutive windows, and each streak fires exactly once.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.BI analyze " file.pcap ..."
Score one or more offline captures. Files are opened before analysis
starts; window keys and alert streaks continue across files, so rotated
captures analyze as one timeline.
.TP
.B watch
Read a pcap stream from stdin. Finished windows close on wall-clock time
while the pipe is quiet, so alerts and SIGHUP handling do not wait for new
packets.
.TP
.B selftest
Synthesize a capture with one clean client and one DGA offender, run the
full pipeline, and verify exactly one alert fires for the offender. Exits
non-zero on failure.
.TP
.B config
Print the default configuration as JSON.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-c ", " \-\-config " " \fIpath\fR
Load the configuration from \fIpath\fR. The attached form
.B \-\-config=path
also works. Default: built-in defaults.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose
Log skipped packets and closed windows (with scores) to stderr.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print the version.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print usage.
.SH CONFIGURATION
A flat JSON object; unknown keys are ignored.
.TP
.I window_seconds
Scoring window length in seconds, at least 1. Default 60.
.TP
.I score_threshold
Window score that counts as bad, in (0, 1]. Default 0.6.
.TP
.I windows_before_alert
Consecutive bad windows before an alert fires. Default 3.
.TP
.I trusted_clients
Array of IPv4 addresses or CIDR subnets that are never scored. Default [].
.TP
.I webhook_url
HTTPS endpoint receiving each alert as a JSON POST; TLS certificates are
verified, redirects are disabled, and delivery runs on a background thread
with a 5 s timeout. Empty disables. Default "".
.SH SIGNALS
.TP
.B SIGHUP
Reload the configuration without dropping the capture. A changed
.I window_seconds
resets in-flight windows and streaks.
.TP
.B SIGINT SIGTERM
Stop reading and score everything already captured before exiting.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success, including a drained shutdown and a closed stdout pipe.
.TP
.B 1
Failure: unreadable input, invalid configuration, a stream that is not a
pcap, or an I/O error.
.TP
.B 2
Usage error.
.SH ALERTS
One JSON object per line:
.PP
{"v":1,"client":"10.0.0.42","window":1700000040,"score":0.90,"reasons":["sustained_dga","nxdomain_burst"],"queries":45,"nxdomains":41,"suspicious":30}
.PP
.B queries
counts questions the client asked;
.B nxdomains
counts NXDOMAIN responses received;
.B suspicious
counts questions whose names scored as high-suspicion.
.SH LIMITATIONS
Ethernet IPv4 UDP/53 only. IPv6, pcapng, VLAN tags, DNS over TLS/HTTPS,
and all but the first question per message are not parsed. Packets are
processed in capture order. Webhook delivery is best-effort; consume
stdout JSONL if you need guaranteed delivery.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR tcpdump (1)
